{"no":71,"id":"visual-disorder","th":"ความผิดปกติของการมองเห็น","en":"Visual disorder","pages":"","g":"neuro","b":{"yb":[{"k":"9.9","o":68,"p":"131–136"}],"bb":[{"k":"หน้า 297","o":188,"p":"326"},{"k":"หน้า 298","o":189,"p":"327"},{"k":"หน้า 299–300","o":190,"p":"328–329"},{"k":"หน้า 301","o":191,"p":"330"},{"k":"หน้า 302","o":192,"p":"331"},{"k":"หน้า 303","o":193,"p":"332"},{"k":"หน้า 304","o":194,"p":"333"}]},"sections":[{"id":"bb-298-exam","h":"Approach to an Eye Exam (Blackbook)","html":"<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b298a\"></div>","src":["bb"]},{"id":"bb-297-anat","h":"Cross section of the eye & acronyms (Blackbook)","html":"<figure><img src=\"symp/img/bb-297-f1.webp\" alt=\"Cross section of the eye: ciliary muscle, ciliary body, cornea, lens, pupil, iris, conjunctiva, vitreous humor, sclera, retina, choroid, fovea, macula, optic disk, optic nerve, retinal blood vessels\"><figcaption>Cross section of the eye — Ciliary Muscle, Ciliary Body, Cornea, Lens, Pupil, Iris, Conjunctiva, Vitreous Humor, Sclera, Retina, Choroid, Fovea, Macula, Optic Disk, Optic Nerve, Retinal Blood Vessels</figcaption></figure><h4>Ophthalmology Acronyms</h4><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Acronym</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>EOM</b></td><td>Extra ocular movements</td></tr><tr><td><b>IOL</b></td><td>Intraocular Lens</td></tr><tr><td><b>IOP</b></td><td>Intraocular Pressure</td></tr><tr><td><b>OD</b></td><td>Oculus Dexter (right eye)</td></tr><tr><td><b>OS</b></td><td>Oculus Sinister (left eye)</td></tr><tr><td><b>OU</b></td><td>Oculus Uterque (both eyes)</td></tr><tr><td><b>PERRLA</b></td><td>Pupils Equal, Round, Reactive to Light &amp; Accommodation</td></tr><tr><td><b>RAPD</b></td><td>Relative Afferent pupillary defect</td></tr><tr><td><b>SLE</b></td><td>Slit Lamp Exam</td></tr><tr><td><b>VA</b></td><td>Visual Acuity</td></tr></tbody></table></div>","src":["bb"]},{"id":"yb-9-9-blur","h":"9.9.1 Blurred vision and visual acuity loss","html":"<p><small>โน้ตลายมือหัวบท 9.9 (ข้างชื่อบท Visual disorder):</small> <span class=\"hw\">stroke ข้ามใช้(?) uptodate แต่ที่ใช้ med scape</span></p><div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"y99a\"></div><p>เมื่อพบผู้ป่วยที่มีอาการมองไม่ชัด (Blurred vision) สิ่งที่สำคัญที่สุดคือการแยกให้ได้ว่าอาการมองไม่ชัดนั้นมีลักษณะอย่างไร ได้แก่ ภาพมัวลง (Reduce visual acuity), มองเห็นด้านข้างไม่ชัดหรือลานประสาทตาแคบลง (Visual field defect), มองเห็นภาพซ้อนเป็นสองภาพ (Diplopia) หรือมองเห็นภาพสั่นไหว (Oscillopsia) เมื่อเราบ่งบอกได้ชัดเจนเราก็จะสามารถหาสืบค้นหาสาเหตุของอาการได้อย่างเป็นระบบ</p><p>ในแผนภาพด้านบน ได้จำแนกสาเหตุของภาวะ visual acuity ลดลงตามสาเหตุตามกายวิภาคศาสตร์ ส่วนแผนภาพในหน้าถัดไปจะแสดงสาเหตุของภาวะ visual acuity ที่ลดลงตามระยะเวลาของการเกิดอาการดังกล่าว</p>","sub":[{"id":"yb-9-9-time","h":"Time based approach to Visual acuity loss","html":"<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"y99b\"></div>","src":["yb"]}],"src":["yb"]},{"id":"bb-299-acute","h":"Acute vision loss (Blackbook)","sub":[{"id":"bb-299-bil","h":"Bilateral","html":"<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b299a\"></div><div class=\"pearl\"><p><b>Clinical Pearl:</b></p><ul><li>Patients with bilateral acute vision loss should have a CT.</li></ul></div>","src":["bb"]},{"id":"bb-299-uni","h":"Unilateral","html":"<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b299b\"></div><div class=\"pearl\"><p><b>Clinical Pearls:</b></p><ul><li>Optic neuritis causes pain with EOM</li><li>Temporal arteritis causes temporalis pain and pain with mastication</li><li>Acute angle closure glaucoma causes high intraocular pressure, unilateral eye pain, mid-dilated pupil and n/v</li><li>Retinal detachment can present as a veil over the vision and with flashes and floaters.</li><li>TIA, vein or artery occlusion requires stroke work-up</li></ul></div>","src":["bb"]}],"src":["bb"]},{"id":"bb-301-chronic","h":"Chronic vision loss — Anatomic (Blackbook)","html":"<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b301a\"></div><div class=\"pearl\"><p><b>Clinical Pearls:</b></p><ul><li>Edema can cause halos in the vision.</li><li>Bilateral disc swelling and any suspected mass require imaging.</li></ul></div>","src":["bb"]},{"id":"bb-302-ambly","h":"Amblyopia (Blackbook)","html":"<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b302a\"></div><p><small>* Can cause permanent visual impairment if not treated urgently in infancy</small></p><div class=\"pearl\"><p><b>Clinical Pearl:</b></p><ul><li>Congenital cataracts and retinoblastoma's cause leukocoria and a decreased red reflex</li></ul></div>","src":["bb"]},{"id":"yb-9-9-dip","h":"9.9.2 Diplopia","html":"<div class=\"sb yb\"><div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"y99c\"></div></div>","sub":[{"id":"yb-9-9-dipcause","h":"Common cause of Binocular Diplopia","html":"<p>จากหน้าที่แล้วจะสังเกตเห็นว่าสาเหตุของ diplopia มีด้วยกันหลายสาเหตุ แผนภาพด้านล่างนี้จะแสดงถึงสาเหตุของภาวะ diplopia ที่พบได้บ่อยในเวชปฏิบัติ</p><div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"y99d\"></div>","src":["yb"]},{"id":"yb-9-9-pain","h":"Painful ophthalmoplegia","html":"<p>ส่วนแผนภาพด้านล่างจะแสดงภาวะที่เรียกว่า painful ophthalmoplegia ซึ่งเป็นอีกภาวะหนึ่งที่พบได้ในเวชปฏิบัติเช่นกัน แต่จะมีกลุ่มโรคที่จะต้องให้ความสำคัญเพิ่มขึ้น โดยรายละเอียดดังแสดงในแผนภาพ</p><div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"y99e\"></div>","src":["yb"]},{"id":"bb-303-scheme","h":"Diplopia scheme (Blackbook)","html":"<div class=\"flow\" data-flow=\"b303a\"></div><div class=\"pearl\"><p><b>Clinical Pearls:</b></p><ul><li>Diplopia is almost always binocular.</li><li>CN VI palsy is a red flag for intracranial masses.</li><li>Look for ptosis with CN III palsy.</li><li>Examine both eyes to determine which is affected.</li><li>Neurologic symptoms suggest a mass as the cause.</li><li>Myasthenia Gravis is fatiguable.</li><li>Migraine is a diagnosis of exclusion.</li></ul></div>","src":["bb"]}],"src":["yb","bb"]},{"id":"yb-9-9-vf","h":"9.9.3 Visual field defect","html":"<div class=\"sb yb\"><figure><img src=\"symp/img/yb-9-9-f6.webp\" alt=\"Visual pathway และ visual field defect จุด 1–4 (central scotoma, blindness ตาขวา, right nasal hemianopia, bitemporal hemianopia)\"><figcaption>Visual pathway: Optic nerve, Optic chiasm, Optic tract, Lateral geniculate body, Optic radiation, Occipital lobe — รอยโรคจุด 1–4 และ visual field ของตาซ้าย (Lt) / ขวา (Rt) ที่สัมพันธ์กัน</figcaption></figure><figure><img src=\"symp/img/yb-9-9-f7.webp\" alt=\"Visual pathway และ visual field defect จุด 5–8 (homonymous hemianopia, quadrantanopia, macular sparing)\"><figcaption>รอยโรคจุด 5–8 (optic tract/radiation/occipital lobe) และ visual field ของตาซ้าย (Lt) / ขวา (Rt)</figcaption></figure><h4>สรุป visual field defect ตามตำแหน่งรอยโรค (จากภาพ)</h4><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>จุด</th><th>ภาพ visual field (Lt / Rt)</th><th>ลักษณะ field defect</th><th>Lesion</th><th>Etiology</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Lt ปกติ · Rt มีจุดดำตรงกลาง</td><td>Central scotoma Rt eye</td><td>Optic disc/Optic nerve Rt</td><td>Optic neuritis/Retrobulbar neuritis</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Lt ปกติ · Rt มืดทั้งวง</td><td>Total blindness of Rt eye</td><td>Complete lesion of optic nerve</td><td>ดูต่อเรื่อง Visual acuity loss</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Lt ปกติ · Rt มืดครึ่งซ้ายของวง (ด้านจมูก)</td><td>Right nasal hemianopia</td><td>Perichiasmal</td><td>calcified internal carotid artery</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Lt มืดครึ่งซ้าย · Rt มืดครึ่งขวา (ด้านขมับทั้งสองตา)</td><td>Bitemporal hemianopia</td><td>Chiasmatic lesion</td><td><ol><li>Pituitary adenoma<ul><li>Functioning: prolactinoma, Corticotrophic adenoma</li><li>Non-functioning</li></ul></li><li>Craniopharyngioma</li><li>Meningioma</li></ol></td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Lt และ Rt มืดครึ่งซ้ายของวงทั้งสองตา</td><td>Left Homonymous hemianopia</td><td>Optic tract Rt or Optic radiation Rt</td><td>Stroke, trauma, tumor of Rt parietal lobe</td></tr><tr><td>6</td><td>Lt และ Rt มืดจตุภาคบนซ้าย</td><td>Left homonymous superior quadrantanopia</td><td>Partial involvement of optic radiation</td><td>Lesion in right temporal lobe</td></tr><tr><td>7</td><td>Lt และ Rt มืดจตุภาคล่างซ้าย</td><td>Left homonymous Inferior quadrantanopia</td><td>Partial involvement of optic radiation</td><td>Lesion in right parietal lobe</td></tr><tr><td>8</td><td>Lt และ Rt มืดครึ่งซ้ายของวง แต่เหลือจุดกลางภาพ (macula) ไว้</td><td>Left homonymous hemianopia with macular sparing</td><td>Occipital lobe lesion</td><td>PCA infarction</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>","sub":[{"id":"bb-304-vf","h":"Visual field defects by lesion site (Blackbook)","html":"<figure><img src=\"symp/img/bb-304-f1.webp\" alt=\"Neuro-ophthalmology visual field defects: hand-drawn visual pathway with lesion sites (optic nerve, optic chiasm, optic tract, lateral geniculate nucleus, Meyer's loop, right parietal lobe) and the corresponding left/right eye visual field circles\"><figcaption>Neuro-Ophthalmology — Visual Field Defects: lesion site on the visual pathway and the matching field defect in the right/left eye (black = lost field)</figcaption></figure><div class=\"tbl\"><table><thead><tr><th>Lesion site</th><th>Visual field defect</th><th>Causes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><b>Optic Nerve Lesion</b></td><td>Monocular vision loss</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><b>Optic Chiasm Lesion</b></td><td>Bitemporal hemianopia</td><td><ul><li>Pituitary/metastatic tumor</li><li>Craniopharyngioma</li><li>Meningioma</li><li>Optic nerve glioma</li><li>Aneurysm</li><li>Infection</li><li>MS</li><li>Sarcoidosis</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td><b>Optic Tract Lesion</b></td><td>Incongruous right homonymous hemianopia</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><b>Lateral Geniculate Nucleus Lesion</b></td><td>Right homonymous horizontal sectoranopia</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><b>Meyer's Loop Lesion</b></td><td>Incongruous superior homonymous quadrantanopia</td><td></td></tr><tr><td><b>Right Parietal Lobe Lesion</b></td><td>Inferior homonymous hemianopia</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div>","src":["bb"]}],"src":["yb","bb"]}],"flows":[{"id":"y99a","title":"Blurred vision","src":"fig","img":"yb-9-9-f1.webp","nodes":[{"id":"a","k":"start","t":"Blurred vision","d":"<p>โน้ตลายมือหัวบท 9.9: <span class=\"hw\">stroke ข้ามใช้(?) uptodate แต่ที่ใช้ med scape</span></p>"},{"id":"b","k":"act","t":"Clarify patient symptoms to medical terminology"},{"id":"vf","k":"q","t":"Visual field defect","d":"<p><b>Hx:</b> มองบางส่วนของภาพไม่เห็น เช่น ด้านข้าง เป็นต้น มีประวัติเดินชนด้านข้าง</p><p><b>PE:</b> Visual field defect</p>"},{"id":"va","k":"q","t":"Visual acuity defect","d":"<p><b>Hx:</b> มองภาพมัวไม่ชัดเหมือนเคยหรือมองไม่เห็นไปเลย (Blindness)</p><p><b>PE:</b> VA <span class=\"down\">↓</span></p>"},{"id":"dp","k":"q","t":"Diplopia","d":"<p><b>Hx:</b> มองเห็นภาพซ้อน คือ มองเห็นวัตถุสิ่งเดียวเป็นสองภาพซ้อนกัน</p><p><b>PE:</b> Abnormal EOM</p>"},{"id":"os","k":"q","t":"Oscillopsia","d":"<p><b>Hx:</b> มองเห็นวัตถุมีการสั่นไหวแม้วัตถุอยู่นิ่ง</p><p><b>PE:</b> nystagmus</p>"},{"id":"vf2","k":"note","t":"ดูต่อเรื่อง Visual field defect","d":"<p>ดูหัวข้อ 9.9.3 Visual field defect</p>"},{"id":"an","k":"q","t":"Anatomical approach"},{"id":"dp2","k":"note","t":"ดูต่อเรื่อง Diplopia","d":"<p>ดูหัวข้อ 9.9.2 Diplopia</p>"},{"id":"os2","k":"dx","t":"Oscillopsia: Cerebellar lesion / Brain stem lesion","d":"<ul><li>Cerebellar lesion</li><li>Brain stem lesion</li></ul>"},{"id":"oc","k":"q","t":"Ocular disorder"},{"id":"ne","k":"q","t":"Neurologic disorder"},{"id":"ant","k":"q","t":"Anterior segment"},{"id":"post","k":"q","t":"Posterior segment"},{"id":"corn","k":"dx","t":"Corneal ulcer"},{"id":"glau","k":"dx","t":"Glaucoma"},{"id":"cat","k":"dx","t":"Cataract"},{"id":"vit","k":"dx","t":"Vitreous humour: Vitreous hemorrhage","d":"<ul><li>Vitreous hemorrhage</li></ul>"},{"id":"ret","k":"dx","t":"Retina: Papilledema, Retinal detachment, Retinal hemorrhage","d":"<ul><li>Papilledema</li><li>Retinal detachment</li><li>Retinal hemorrhage</li></ul>"},{"id":"rv","k":"dx","t":"Retinal vascular: CRAO, CRVO, Hypoperfusion, Hyperviscosity","d":"<ul><li>CRAO</li><li>CRVO</li><li>Hypoperfusion<ul><li>Embolic</li><li>BP <span class=\"down\">↓</span></li></ul></li><li>Hyperviscosity</li></ul>"},{"id":"on","k":"dx","t":"Optic n. lesion: Optic neuritis, AION, PION","d":"<ul><li>Optic neuritis</li><li>AION</li><li>PION</li></ul>"},{"id":"occ","k":"dx","t":"Occipital lobe lesion: PRES, Stroke, Tumor","d":"<ul><li>PRES</li><li>Stroke</li><li>Tumor</li></ul>"}],"edges":[{"f":"a","t":"b"},{"f":"b","t":"vf","l":"Visual field defect"},{"f":"b","t":"va","l":"Visual acuity defect"},{"f":"b","t":"dp","l":"Diplopia"},{"f":"b","t":"os","l":"Oscillopsia"},{"f":"vf","t":"vf2"},{"f":"va","t":"an"},{"f":"dp","t":"dp2"},{"f":"os","t":"os2"},{"f":"an","t":"oc","l":"Ocular disorder"},{"f":"an","t":"ne","l":"Neurologic disorder"},{"f":"oc","t":"ant","l":"Anterior segment"},{"f":"oc","t":"post","l":"Posterior segment"},{"f":"ant","t":"corn","l":"Cornea"},{"f":"ant","t":"glau","l":"Anterior chamber"},{"f":"ant","t":"cat","l":"Lens"},{"f":"post","t":"vit","l":"Vitreous humour"},{"f":"post","t":"ret","l":"Retina"},{"f":"post","t":"rv","l":"Retinal vascular"},{"f":"ne","t":"on","l":"Optic n. lesion"},{"f":"ne","t":"occ","l":"Occipital lobe lesion"}],"note":"ลายมือหัวบท: stroke ... uptodate ... med scape (ใส่ไว้ที่กล่องเริ่มต้น)","book":"yb"},{"id":"y99b","title":"Time based approach to Visual acuity loss","src":"fig","img":"yb-9-9-f2.webp","nodes":[{"id":"a","k":"start","t":"Time based approach to Visual acuity loss"},{"id":"sud","k":"q","t":"Sudden visual loss","d":"<p>การมองเห็นแย่ลงอย่างเฉียบพลัน</p>"},{"id":"pro","k":"q","t":"Progressive visual loss","d":"<p>การมองเห็นแย่ลงเรื่อยๆ</p>"},{"id":"tr","k":"q","t":"Transient","d":"<p>การมองเห็นแย่ลงอย่างเฉียบพลันแต่ต่อมากลับมามองเห็นได้ปกติ</p>"},{"id":"np","k":"q","t":"Without progression","d":"<p>การมองเห็นแย่ลงอย่างเฉียบพลันโดยไม่กลับมาเป็นปกติเอง</p>"},{"id":"trm","k":"q","t":"Transient: Monocular"},{"id":"trb","k":"dx","t":"Transient binocular","d":"<ul><li>Cerebral hypoperfusion</li><li>PRES</li><li>Seizure</li><li>Head trauma</li><li>Visual obscuration (Papilledema)</li><li>Migraine</li></ul>"},{"id":"bs","k":"dx","t":"Blood supply <span class=\"down\">↓</span> to retina","d":"<ul><li>Embolic CVD (Amaurosis fugax)</li><li>Hypoperfusion<ul><li>BP <span class=\"down\">↓</span></li><li>Hyperviscosity</li></ul></li><li>Vascular disease<ul><li>Vasospasm</li><li>Vasculitis</li></ul></li></ul>"},{"id":"oth","k":"dx","t":"Other: Migraine, AACG, Impending CRVO","d":"<ul><li>Migraine</li><li>AACG</li><li>Impending CRVO</li></ul>"},{"id":"npm","k":"q","t":"Without progression: Monocular"},{"id":"npb","k":"dx","t":"Without progression: Binocular","d":"<ul><li>Bilat ION</li><li>Pituitary apoplexy</li><li>Occipital lobe stroke</li><li>Head trauma</li><li>Functional</li></ul>"},{"id":"vas","k":"dx","t":"Vascular d/o: CRAO, CRVO, AION, PION","d":"<ul><li>CRAO</li><li>CRVO</li><li>AION</li><li>PION</li></ul>"},{"id":"rtn","k":"dx","t":"Retina d/o: Retinal detachment, Serous retinopathy","d":"<ul><li>Retinal detachment</li><li>Serous retinopathy</li></ul>"},{"id":"opt","k":"dx","t":"Optic n. d/o: TON","d":"<ul><li>TON</li></ul>"},{"id":"vh","k":"dx","t":"Vitreous hemorrhage"},{"id":"inf","k":"dx","t":"Ant visual pathway inflammation","d":"<ul><li>Optic neuritis</li><li>Sarcoidosis</li><li>meningitis</li><li>Radiation</li></ul>"},{"id":"cmp","k":"dx","t":"Ant visual pathway compression","d":"<ul><li>Tumor</li><li>Aneurysm</li><li>Thyroid-ass. orbitopathy</li></ul>"},{"id":"gl","k":"dx","t":"Glaucoma"},{"id":"cp","k":"dx","t":"Chronic papilledema"},{"id":"tox","k":"dx","t":"Toxic","d":"<ul><li>Ethambutol</li></ul>"},{"id":"par","k":"dx","t":"Paraneoplastic retinopathy"}],"edges":[{"f":"a","t":"sud"},{"f":"a","t":"pro"},{"f":"sud","t":"tr","l":"Transient"},{"f":"sud","t":"np","l":"Without progression"},{"f":"tr","t":"trm","l":"Monocular"},{"f":"tr","t":"trb","l":"Binocular"},{"f":"trm","t":"bs","l":"Blood supply ↓ to retina"},{"f":"trm","t":"oth","l":"Other"},{"f":"np","t":"npm","l":"Monocular"},{"f":"np","t":"npb","l":"Binocular"},{"f":"npm","t":"vas","l":"Vascular d/o"},{"f":"npm","t":"rtn","l":"Retina d/o"},{"f":"npm","t":"opt","l":"Optic n. d/o"},{"f":"npm","t":"vh","l":"Vitreous hemorrhage"},{"f":"pro","t":"inf","l":"Ant visual pathway inflammation"},{"f":"pro","t":"cmp","l":"Ant visual pathway compression"},{"f":"pro","t":"gl","l":"Glaucoma"},{"f":"pro","t":"cp","l":"Chronic papilledema"},{"f":"pro","t":"tox","l":"Toxic"},{"f":"pro","t":"par","l":"Paraneoplastic retinopathy"}],"book":"yb"},{"id":"y99c","title":"Diplopia","src":"fig","img":"yb-9-9-f3.webp","nodes":[{"id":"a","k":"start","t":"Diplopia"},{"id":"hx","k":"act","t":"Hx ที่สำคัญ","d":"<ol><li>Monocular v.s. Binocular</li><li>Vertical v.s. Horizontal</li><li>Directionality (มองไปทางใดแล้วภาพซ้อนมากขึ้น เช่น บน/ล่าง/ซ้าย/ขวา)</li></ol>"},{"id":"pe","k":"act","t":"PE ที่สำคัญ","d":"<ol><li>Eye misalignment/Ptosis/Pupils</li><li>EOM: Full, Vergence?</li><li>Saccade/Pursuit eye movement</li><li>Face/Ocular abnormality</li><li>Oculocephalic maneuver</li></ol>"},{"id":"s","k":"q","t":"Monocular หรือ Binocular diplopia?"},{"id":"mono","k":"q","t":"Monocular diplopia","d":"<p>มีภาพซ้อนแม้มองด้วยตาข้างเดียว</p>"},{"id":"bino","k":"q","t":"Binocular diplopia","d":"<p>มองเห็นภาพซ้อนเมื่อมองด้วยสองตา แต่ถ้ามองด้วยตาข้างเดียวจะไม่ซ้อน</p>"},{"id":"oph","k":"dx","t":"Ophthalmic: Macula abnormality"},{"id":"neu","k":"dx","t":"Neurologic","d":"<ul><li>Occipital lobe lesion</li><li>Drug induce visual hallucination</li></ul>"},{"id":"fun","k":"dx","t":"Functional"},{"id":"dis","k":"q","t":"Disconjugated eye","d":"<p>ตาสองข้างวางตัวคนละระดับกัน (Misalignment)</p>"},{"id":"nd","k":"q","t":"Neurologic disorder"},{"id":"orb","k":"dx","t":"Orbital processing causing diplopia","d":"<ul><li>Orbital floor fracture</li><li>Muscle infiltration</li><li>Orbital myositis/ Orbital pseudotumor</li><li>Thyroid associated ophthalmopathy</li></ul>"},{"id":"cs","k":"dx","t":"Congenital strabismus","d":"<ul><li>Esotropia</li><li>Exotropia</li></ul>"},{"id":"sup","k":"dx","t":"Supranuclear: INO"},{"i